{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"single-vast-roan","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context\n\nUse the portable shadow corpus as the prerequisite for live differential evidence, then complete the typed reconciler migration in this story. Legacy deletion is a completion condition, not deferred cleanup.\n\nReuse the existing real Jira 8.17.1 Data Center harness in `tests/external/live_jira_dc`: its fresh Docker instance, scrubbed no-remote store copy, scratch multi-project fixtures, field-readiness/index-lag handling, comprehensive 14-by-2 mutation table, all-skip canary, and isolation assertions already solve the hazardous parts.\n\n## Work\n\n- Add an exact-patchset CI entry to the existing DC harness so the implementation under review—not only merged `main`—can be exercised.\n- Compare legacy and typed behavior only on isolated projects or fresh instances. Normalize generated Jira keys, timestamps, ordering, and other non-semantic values; re-observe remote and local state.\n- Exercise representative real-store volume while scoping writes so copied unbound tickets cannot be filed en masse.\n- After parity, flip the one production route to typed payloads/adapters and delete the compatibility paths in the same epic.\n- Rerun a typed-only live convergence/idempotence pass after deletion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] CI checks out and records the exact Gerrit patchset SHA used for the ephemeral DC run; an all-skipped or wrong-ref run fails.\n- [ ] Both outer and ticket-store repos have no remotes, `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off`, Cloud/live-project credentials are absent, and every Jira target is a disposable harness project or instance.\n- [ ] Legacy and typed runs never write the same issue. Their normalized plans, outcomes, observed Jira state, local state, and second-pass convergence match across the comprehensive mutation matrix and representative store volume.\n- [ ] The typed-only post-cutover DC run converges twice without duplicate effects, lost fields, cross-project contamination, or unexplained diagnostics.\n- [ ] Portable/default CI remains authoritative when Docker/DC is unavailable; the live lane is additive evidence.\n- [ ] Production no longer converts typed mutations to dictionaries or selects behavior by `apply()` argument shape.\n- [ ] `_mutation_to_batch_dict`, duplicate CREATE shapes, obsolete legacy batch leaves/facades, and test-only compatibility re-exports with no supported consumers are deleted; remaining compatibility is explicitly public and justified.\n- [ ] Full reconciler suites, default suite, lint, typecheck, and the exact-patchset DC lane pass before the story closes.","id":"3f27-cb3c-8023-4f57","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["reconciler","jira-dc","cutover"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Prove Jira DC parity, cut over the reconciler, and delete legacy dispatch"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788026447197550251,"uuid":"90559721-d7bd-45aa-a6e3-1572679095ea"}